Roast.pet Weird Builder Projects =E2=80=94 4 useful new finds

This pass screened 25+ plausible projects/results across GitHub,
Hugging Face, pet re-identification, browser-native video, POD
mockups, Etsy tooling and adjacent technical projects. Prior Roast.pet
scanner discoveries were excluded. Four survived the no-padding bar.

1) Open Noodle Gallery Pet Recognition =E2=80=94 REUSE NOW / FORK THE MODEL

URL: https://opennoodle.de/features/pet-recognition/ and
https://github.com/open-noodle/gallery

Creator: Open Noodle

Activity: v5.6.0 release candidate published September 5, 2026;
Gallery repo currently ~374 stars.

License: Pet recognition weights Apache-2.0; Gallery application AGPL-3.0.

This is the strongest find of the run. Open Noodle has just released
three pet re-identification models specifically for distinguishing
individual dogs and cats. They are frozen DINOv2 backbones plus a
trained linear projection producing a 512-dimensional normalized
embedding. Crucially, the weights are openly published under
Apache-2.0 and the complete training/evaluation/ONNX-export pipeline
is committed.

Training data is commercially much cleaner than several earlier
pet-identity finds: Dogs-World provides 313,688 photos of 126,550
individual dogs under CC0; Cat Individual Images provides 13,536
photos under CC BY. DogFaceNet is held out entirely for evaluation.
The split is by identity, not image.

Published unseen-identity Top-1 results:

- small (~89 MB, DINOv2-S): dogs 0.535, cats 0.913

- base (~348 MB, DINOv2-B): dogs 0.612, cats 0.916

- large (~1.2 GB, DINOv2-L): dogs 0.672, cats 0.915

The authors also publish the less flattering full-split result after
discovering an earlier sampled evaluation was optimistic. This is
unusually good evidence hygiene.

Roast.pet step solved: a commercially usable candidate for the
pet-identity embedding in our identity firewall. Instead of
inventing/training an embedding now, canonical customer photos can be
embedded once and every generated reaction compared by cosine
distance.

Install/API route: use the published open-noodle pet-recognition
weights / ONNX path from Gallery rather than adopting the AGPL
application.

Dependencies/hardware: DINOv2 backbone; model size determines compute.
Small is the obvious first benchmark.

Evidence: full held-out identity evaluation; open weights; production
integration in Gallery; RF-DETR pet detection underneath reportedly
raised species recall from 84.8% to 98.1%.

Code/work replaced: potentially weeks of pet metric-learning/data
sourcing/evaluation work and removes the licensing uncertainty around
DogFLW/PetFace-derived production models.

Integration difficulty: MEDIUM.

Maintenance risk: LOW-MEDIUM; pin weights and embedding version
because embedding spaces are incompatible across model changes.

Exact experiment: 30 customer-style pets =C3=97 3 source photos; generate 5
acceptable transformations and 5 deliberate identity-drift
transformations each. Compare small/base embeddings against our
geometry and nose-biometric candidates. Measure ROC/AUC and choose an
ACCEPT / REVIEW / REJECT threshold. Also test whether multi-photo
centroid enrollment materially improves dog accuracy.

Verdict: REUSE NOW / FORK MODEL PIPELINE.

2) LocalCut Studio =E2=80=94 COPY/REUSE THE BROWSER MEDIA ENGINE

URL: https://github.com/shenghaoc/localcut

Creator: shenghaoc

Activity: 163 commits; crawled current September 20, 2026; 1 star / 0 forks=
.

License: MIT.

This is exactly the weird-builder profile we want: essentially no
popularity, but an enormous amount of solved browser-media plumbing.
LocalCut is a complete browser-native NLE using WebCodecs, WebGPU,
workers, SharedArrayBuffer and Mediabunny. It supports multi-track
video/audio/images, titles, captions, transforms, keyframes, effects,
audio mixing, H.264/MP4, VP9/WebM and AV1/WebM export, IndexedDB/OPFS
persistence and offline PWA operation.

The important part is engineering maturity rather than editor UI:
2,504 passing Node tests across 225 files plus real-browser and
Playwright testing; explicit capability tiers; runtime codec/GPU
probes; deterministic VideoFrame cleanup; worker-owned
decode/encode/pixel work; and graceful Canvas2D/WebCodecs fallbacks.

Roast.pet step solved: almost every ugly browser-native
composition/export detail behind interactive roast preview and local
rendering.

Install/demo route: clone repo, install with its documented package
tooling, run dev; live deployment is linked from README.

Dependencies/hardware: modern browser; best path requires WebGPU +
WebCodecs + OffscreenCanvas + SharedArrayBuffer/cross-origin
isolation. Reduced WebCodecs/Canvas paths exist.

Evidence: live deployment, 163 commits, extensive tests and explicit
supported/experimental boundaries.

Code/work replaced: potentially thousands of lines of WebCodecs/WebGPU
worker, muxing, capability-detection, project-storage and
caption/export infrastructure.

Integration difficulty: MEDIUM if extracting engine pieces; HIGH if
adopting editor wholesale.

Maintenance risk: MEDIUM. Desktop-first; mobile Safari is not the
target full-performance path.

Exact experiment: reproduce one canonical 15-second Roast.pet clip
using only LocalCut primitives: background, canonical pet
PNG/animation, TTS, captions, sting, title card. Export 9:16 H.264 and
WebM in Chrome on a weak laptop. Record render time, memory and exact
unsupported features. Do not integrate UI.

Verdict: COPY ENGINE MECHANISMS / BENCHMARK NOW.

3) Velocut =E2=80=94 WATCH / COPY THE AGENT-EDITING PROTOCOL

URL: https://github.com/open-ribbi/velocut

Creator: Ribbi / open-ribbi

Activity: release 0.0.2 current; ~450 stars; active 2026 project.

License: MIT; bundled third-party assets retain their own licenses.

Velocut overlaps LocalCut as a browser renderer/editor, but its unique
Roast.pet value is different: humans and agents modify the exact same
project through a typed JSON command protocol with revision checks,
branching history and undo. It exposes separate provider, protocol,
timeline/core, render, scene, runtime, MCP and CLI packages. It also
persists asynchronous video-generation jobs and lets generated
candidates be previewed/adopted into timeline slots without
resubmitting after reload.

Roast.pet step solved: the internal representation for agent-directed
roast assembly and generation experiments. Instead of hard-coding
=E2=80=98make a roast video=E2=80=99 as a monolithic function, a roast can =
be a
versioned document receiving deterministic commands from
workers/agents.

Install: npx @velocut/cli@0.0.2 studio; SDK packages are independently
installable.

Dependencies/hardware: Node 22.6+; full editor currently Chrome/Edge
with WebGPU/WebCodecs. Safari/Firefox unsupported for full editor.

Evidence: release packages, SDKs, CI across Rust/TS engines and editor
journeys, documented durable provider-job lifecycle.

Code/work replaced: command protocol, undo/history, stale-write
rejection, provider-job lifecycle, project persistence and agent
editing bridge.

Integration difficulty: MEDIUM-HIGH if adopted; LOW to copy protocol ideas.

Maintenance risk: MEDIUM-HIGH because 0.0.x and fast-moving.

Exact experiment: represent one Roast.pet performance.json + media
assets as a Velocut project and have an agent make three changes
(=E2=80=98move punchline 400 ms earlier=E2=80=99, =E2=80=98make caption lar=
ger=E2=80=99, =E2=80=98replace
reaction clip=E2=80=99) through commands. Confirm history, deterministic
replay and stale-edit rejection.

Verdict: WATCH / COPY MECHANISM, not a production dependency yet.

4) automated_mockups =E2=80=94 REUSE NOW FOR SIMPLE POD LISTING IMAGES

URL: https://github.com/CTDave001/automated_mockups

Creator: CTDave001

Activity: 29 commits, 73 stars, 19 forks.

License: MIT.

This small Python package does one boring thing well: batch overlays
every design onto every product template. Instead of requiring PSD
smart objects, templates contain a colored placeholder region; the
tool detects its position/size/rotation once, stores parameters, and
then generates all combinations in parallel. It supports
PNG/JPEG/WebP, nine alignments, rotation, CLI and Python API.

Roast.pet step solved: deterministic listing mockups for simple
card/poster/T-shirt scenes where photorealistic deformation is
unnecessary. This is a better default than introducing Photoshop
automation.

Install: pip install mockup-generator or clone/install editable.

Dependencies: Python 3.8+, NumPy, Pillow, scikit-image, OpenCV. CPU.

Evidence: packaged CLI/API, tests/examples, 73 stars and 19 forks.

Code/work replaced: template-coordinate tooling, batch loops, image
compositing and parallelization.

Integration difficulty: LOW.

Maintenance risk: LOW.

Exact experiment: prepare 5 Roast.pet templates (card front, framed
card, tee front, poster, social listing shot), mark print regions, and
run 20 fake pet designs through all five. Compare generated output
against current manual mockups for placement accuracy and total
runtime.

Verdict: REUSE NOW for deterministic simple mockups; keep AI lifestyle
mockups separate.

Important adjacency: Etsy listing video API trap

A current September 5, 2026 technical report notes that Etsy=E2=80=99s UI n=
ow
allows two listing videos, while the public v3 write endpoint still
behaves as a one-video path. Separately, Etsy=E2=80=99s own GitHub discussi=
on
documents that a video_id already attached to one listing cannot
reliably be reused on another despite documentation suggesting
otherwise. For Roast.pet, assume every listing owns its uploaded video
and automate one API video per listing; treat any second video as a
manual/UI-only enhancement until API parity changes.

TOP 5 THINGS WE SHOULD NOT BUILD OURSELVES

- A pet identity embedding from scratch before benchmarking Open
Noodle=E2=80=99s Apache-2.0 DINOv2 pet models.

- Browser codec/GPU capability detection, worker decode/encode and mux
plumbing =E2=80=94 LocalCut has already accumulated this pain.

- Generic timeline command/history/undo infrastructure for agent video
editing =E2=80=94 Velocut already demonstrates a typed protocol.

- Simple POD mockup placement/batch generation =E2=80=94 automated_mockups
already packages it.

- Etsy logic that assumes listing videos are reusable assets or that
the API matches the two-video UI.

Most surprising hobby project

LocalCut. One GitHub star hides 163 commits, 2,500+ tests,
WebGPU/WebCodecs composition, captions, export, workers, browser
capability tiers and offline project storage. This is precisely the
kind of repo the scanner is intended to uncover.

Fastest integration win

Open Noodle pet-recognition-small. Download the Apache-2.0 weight,
embed a small canonical/generated pet benchmark and determine in one
experiment whether it becomes the first layer of Roast.pet=E2=80=99s identi=
ty
firewall. It directly attacks one of our genuinely proprietary-risk
problems rather than another UI convenience.

Repo/author worth following

Open Noodle / Gallery. They are actively training and publishing
pet-specific identity models with clean(er) open-data provenance, full
evaluation and ONNX export. That is unusually aligned with Roast.pet,
and the September 2026 release is fresh enough that further pet-CV
improvements are plausible.

Architectural implication

The identity firewall can now become much more concrete:

canonical photos =E2=86=92 Open Noodle 512-D embedding centroid + pet geome=
try
+ optional nose biometric =E2=86=92 generated reaction =E2=86=92 same measu=
rements =E2=86=92
weighted ACCEPT / REVIEW / REJECT.

If the open model works, Roast.pet does not need to become a
pet-recognition research lab. Our accumulating moat becomes the
production dataset of which generated transformations humans
accepted/rejected for a specific real pet, while the underlying
embedding model remains replaceable.
